.TH "REPROCTL\-COMPLETION" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-completion \- generate shell completion scripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl completion\f[R] \f[I]shell\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate shell completion scripts for reproctl.
The completion script is written to stdout so it can be redirected to a
file or evaluated directly.
.PP
When run without a shell argument, installation instructions are printed
to stderr.
.SS Supported shells
.TP
\f[B]bash\f[R]
Bash completion using the bash\-completion framework.
.TP
\f[B]zsh\f[R]
Zsh completion using the compdef/compsys framework.
.TP
\f[B]fish\f[R]
Fish completion using the \f[B]complete\f[R] builtin.
.SH INSTALLATION
.SS Bash
Write to the bash\-completion directory:
.IP
.EX
reproctl completion bash > \(ti/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/reproctl
.EE
.PP
Or eval in \f[B]\(ti/.bashrc\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
eval \(dq$(reproctl completion bash)\(dq
.EE
.SS Zsh
Write to a directory in \f[B]fpath\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
reproctl completion zsh > \(dq${fpath[1]}/_reproctl\(dq && compinit
.EE
.PP
Or eval in \f[B]\(ti/.zshrc\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
eval \(dq$(reproctl completion zsh)\(dq
.EE
.SS Fish
Write to the fish completions directory:
.IP
.EX
reproctl completion fish > \(ti/.config/fish/completions/reproctl.fish
.EE
.PP
Or eval directly:
.IP
.EX
reproctl completion fish | source
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl completion bash
Print the Bash completion script to stdout.
.TP
reproctl completion zsh > /usr/local/share/zsh/site\-functions/_reproctl
Install Zsh completions system\-wide.
.TP
reproctl completion fish | source
Load Fish completions in the current session.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]reproctl\f[R](1)
